{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778938076,"nonce":"D8xNRjDbKaq7eivGy4q646UmDuI=","message":"## Additional constraint: avoid repo-lock coupling\n\nThe Mandible-native issue/work ledger should be designed so normal issue reads/writes do not depend on `git-bug`'s per-repo lock. Lock contention is already a recurring operational failure mode, so the new backend should make local Mandible operations independent of Git-Bug refs except during explicit import/export/sync jobs.\n\nDesign implications:\n- Mandible issue create/comment/status/metadata updates should write to Mandible's own store first.\n- Git-Bug import/export should run as isolated, retryable sync work with clear status and failure reporting.\n- A stuck Git-Bug lock should not block viewing or updating Mandible-native issues.\n- Sync jobs should be idempotent and resumable so failed imports/exports do not leave ambiguous state.\n- Git-Bug compatibility should be an adapter boundary, not a dependency in the hot path for the canonical ledger.","files":null}]}